The [content-visibility](CSS-CONTAIN-2#propdef-content-visibility) property controls whether or not an element renders its contents at all, along with forcing a strong set of [containments](CSS-CONTAIN-2#containment), allowing user agents to potentially omit large swathes of layout and rendering work until it becomes needed. It has the following values:

**visible** 

No effect. The element’s contents are laid out and rendered as normal.

